.TH MUSIC-CLI 1 "2026-11-22" "JulAIn Music Player 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
music-cli \- JulAIn Music Player: chat with your local music library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B music-cli
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.br
.B music-cli
.B chat
.RB [ \-\-web ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-llm ]
.RI [ "one sentence" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B music-cli
is the command line and window front end of JulAIn Music Player (JMP).
It indexes a music folder you already own, plays it through
.BR mpv (1),
and turns English or German sentences into journalled actions: playback,
playlists, mood and sound rankings, lyrics, library statistics and settings.
.PP
The player never deletes audio and never moves a file without writing a
journal entry first.  Music only enters through a local
.B add
or, in a build that includes an optional download module, through that
module.
.PP
Run
.B music-cli chat --web
to open the window, or
.B music-cli chat
for the terminal interface.  The first run needs a library: a folder with
.BR Playlists/ " and either " Artists/ " or " library-work/ .
Point the launcher at it with the
.B MUSIC_LIBRARY
environment variable or
.IR ~/.config/jmp/library .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B play \fIpath|playlist|search\fR
Play a file, a playlist name or the best search hit.
Options: \fB\-\-append\fR, \fB\-\-shuffle\fR, \fB\-\-first\fR.
.TP
.B pause, resume, toggle, stop, next, prev
Transport controls for the running mpv daemon.
.TP
.BI seek " [+|\-]SECONDS"
Seek relative to the playhead.
.TP
.BI vol " PERCENT"
Set the volume.
.TP
.B status
Print what is playing.
.TP
.BI search " WORDS"
Search artist, title, album, genre, grouping and path.
.TP
.BI pl " list|show|new|add|remove|delete|check"
Inspect and edit playlists.  Writes are journalled.
.TP
.BI mood " [plan|build|list|play NAME]"
Build and play the measured mood lists.
.TP
.B index
Scan the library, rebuild the reports and the generated playlists.
.TP
.BI data " status|fingerprint|export|import|backup"
The daily plain-text library backup and its import.
.TP
.BI chat " [message]"
The conversational front end.  \fB\-\-web\fR opens the window, \fB\-\-plain\fR
the line interface, \fB\-\-no\-llm\fR forces the offline parser and
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR only plans.
.TP
.B verify
Check that the playlists still resolve and that the library is intact.
.TP
.B shell
Open a shell in the library folder.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MUSIC_LIBRARY
The library folder.  Overrides the discovery and the config files.
.TP
.B MPV_SOCKET
The mpv JSON IPC socket.  The launcher defaults to
.IR /tmp/mpv\-UID.sock .
.TP
.B MUSIC_LLM_CONFIG
An optional planner configuration file (server, model, key); usually set in
the window under Settings.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/jmp/library
One line: the music folder to use.
.TP
.I /etc/jmp/library
The same, system-wide (a user setting wins).
.TP
.I /usr/lib/jmp
The installed application and its documentation.
.TP
.I LIBRARY/library-work
The inventory, journals and caches of a prepared library.
.TP
.I LIBRARY/Playlists
The canonical \fB.m3u8\fR playlists.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
music-cli chat --web
music-cli play Bands
music-cli chat "songs about the sea that are calm"
music-cli search "die ärzte"
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mpv (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1)
.PP
The full manual, the architecture page and the licence audit are installed
under
.IR /usr/share/doc/jmp-ai-music-player/ .
